From: hunterthelabguy <301055645+hunterthelabguy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:00:36 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] F1: pin the label's own zero spacing (mechanical,
 optional)

Not needed to proceed. A label whose direct spacing after was 200, or
removed (the style's 79 then applies), passed every test at T1 as written;
Word would draw a gap between the label's tint and its box. One assertion
in test_word_box_is_the_modern_block; fails on both mutants, green on the
build.
---
 tests/test_downloads.py | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tests/test_downloads.py b/tests/test_downloads.py
index 422724f..d093a57 100644
--- a/tests/test_downloads.py
+++ b/tests/test_downloads.py
@@ -354,6 +354,8 @@ class MarkdownAndWord(unittest.TestCase):
                     self.assertIn('<w:tblW w:w="{}" w:type="dxa"/>'.format(page - left - right), tbl)
                     self.assertRegex(para, r'<w:left w:val="single" w:sz="24"(?=[^>]*\bw:color="{}")'.format(edge))
                     self.assertRegex(para, r'<w:shd\b(?=[^>]*\bw:fill="{}")'.format(behind))
+                    # The sum above assumes the label has no space of its own.
+                    self.assertIn('<w:spacing w:before="0" w:after="0"/>', para)
                     for side in ("top", "right"):
                         self.assertRegex(para, r'<w:{} w:val="single"(?=[^>]*\bw:color="{}")'.format(side, behind))
                     top = re.search(r'<w:top w:val="single" w:sz="(\d+)" w:space="(\d+)"', para)
